<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Reward training</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section presents the loss landscape in the reward modeling.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F13" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F13.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2507.06419v1/figures/losses/PKU_Reward_Loss.png" id="A4.F13.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/250;" width="476" height="250" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F13.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="A4.F13.sf1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">PKU beavertails reward training</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F13.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2507.06419v1/figures/losses/Anthropic_HH_Reward_Loss.png" id="A4.F13.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/250;" width="476" height="250" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F13.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="A4.F13.sf2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Anthropic HH reward training</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F13.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 13</span>: </span><span id="A4.F13.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> <span id="A4.F13.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training loss landscape in reward learning</span>: Here we used LORA adaptors with <math id="A4.F13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=1024</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.F13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=2048" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2048</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=2048</annotation></semantics></math>. We used a Mistral 7B model based reward model.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>DPO </h3>

<figure id="A4.F14" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A4.F14.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2507.06419v1/x20.png" id="A4.F14.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/340;" width="476" height="340" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F14.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="A4.F14.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Utility of the generation (lower score the better)</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A4.F14.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2507.06419v1/x21.svg" id="A4.F14.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/340;" width="476" height="340"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F14.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="A4.F14.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Readability of the generation (closer the distribution better)</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A4.F14.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2507.06419v1/x22.png" id="A4.F14.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/340;" width="476" height="340" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F14.sf3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(c)</span> </span><span id="A4.F14.sf3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Diversity of the generation (higher the better)</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F14.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 14</span>: </span><span id="A4.F14.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> <span id="A4.F14.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Quality of the finetuned reward in DPO (HH)</span>: Figure shows the quality of the reward model finetuned with our augmentations in best of DPO alignment. Alignment with the finetuned reward preserves the readability and the quality of the generation similar to the original reward model (albeit slightly better). In terms of diversity while there was a slight decrease on both the diversity measures with REFORM reward. Here <math id="A4.F14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math> generations were drawn for a given input with the a sampling temperature of <math id="A4.F14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.6</annotation></semantics></math> and the diversity was measured among them. </span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Textual Results</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide textual examples of failure modes, generation, etc.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>False negative counter examples (Ours)</h3>

<figure id="A5.T3" class="ltx_table">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure ltx_flex_table">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="A5.T3.3" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel"><span id="A5.T3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">** This table may contain offensive texts **</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"></p></div></div>
